WEBVTT

00:01:58.615 --> 00:02:02.719
It sparked a curiosity in me
about perceptions that we have

00:02:02.753 --> 00:02:04.921
for women versus men.

00:02:04.955 --> 00:02:10.093
I wanted to know why do we perceive women
differently when we assert ourselves.

00:02:10.127 --> 00:02:12.863
So I did a little research
and I came across something,

00:02:12.863 --> 00:02:15.499
just to make sure
this wasn't all on my mind,

00:02:15.532 --> 00:02:18.001
called the competence/likability dilemma,

00:02:18.035 --> 00:02:20.270
where women, unlike men,

00:02:20.303 --> 00:02:24.341
are rarely perceived
to be both competent and likable.

00:02:24.374 --> 00:02:27.110
Now we should take a moment
to define the word "likable."

00:02:27.110 --> 00:02:29.212
Merriam-Webster says "likeable" is:

00:02:29.246 --> 00:02:32.516
"having qualities that bring about
a favorable regard,